styles=getSampleStyleSheet();story=[]
def clean(txt):
 txt=re.sub(r'(?<=\d)(?=[a-z])',' ',txt)
 txt=re.sub(r'(?<![A-Za-z0-9])(\d+)(?=[A-Z])',r'\1 ',txt)
 txt=re.sub(r'(?<=[a-z])(?=\d)',' ',txt)
 txt=re.sub(r'(?<=[a-z])(?=[A-Z]{2})',' ',txt)
 txt=re.sub(r'([,;:])(?=\S)',r'\1 ',txt)
 return txt
def para(txt,style='Normal'):
 txt=clean(txt)
 doc.add_paragraph(txt,style if style in doc.styles else None);story.append(Paragraph(html.escape(txt),styles['BodyText']));story.append(Spacer(1,5))
def heading(txt,level=1):
 txt=clean(txt)
 doc.add_heading(txt,level);story.append(Paragraph(html.escape(txt),styles['Heading'+str(min(level,3))]));story.append(Spacer(1,5))
def tab(headers,rows):
 t=doc.add_table(rows=1,cols=len(headers));t.style='Light Shading Accent 1'
 for c,x in zip(t.rows[0].cells,headers):c.text=str(x)
 for row in rows:
  for c,x in zip(t.add_row().cells,row):c.text=''if x is None else str(x)
 # Narrative PDF uses compact row paragraphs for legibility.
 for row in rows:story.append(Paragraph(html.escape(' | '.join(str(x)for x in row)),styles['BodyText']));story.append(Spacer(1,3))
heading('Integrated project execution and management package',1)
para('ONGC Mumbai High Bridge Refurbishment & Replacement Project | Tender ZW1PC26002 | Shivansh |25October2026 | P14 Rev0')
para('Issue purpose: management development and review. This issue consolidates requirements, accountable workstreams, operational registers and a reproducible schedule scenario. It does not certify completed structural design, executed procurement/construction, approved AFC drawings or an accepted contract baseline. Actual commencement, resource commitments, productivity, quotations, progress and approvals remain unverified.')
heading('Executive decision brief')
para('The source set supports developing a disciplined EPC control system. It does not establish a fully funded and resource-proven12month execution plan. The previous207activity XML had124links,83activities without predecessors,83without successors and17isolated tasks, and contained no resource assignments. The supplied Gantt image does not supply enough activity/logic detail to validate it.')
para('P14 provides285linked activities with explicit calendars and proposed resource queues. Using an assumed1November2026 start, sequential engineering reviews,45calendar-day steel lead times, two fabrication bays at4MT/productive bay-day, one coating cell and the stated offshore-season planning exclusion, calculated completion is6April2028. This is157calendar days beyond the assumed1November2027 anniversary, before considering any qualifying contractual relief. It is not an actual delay/LD determination.')
para('The driving chain passes through survey/basis acceptance, BHS analysis/detail approvals, steel supply, fabrication-bay queues, coating queues, the final strengthening package, offshore service/removal/punch work and turnover. Additional fabrication capacity alone moves the scenario to26February2028; reducing steel lead time as well does not improve that finish under these other constraints. Review logic, first releases, coating/service capacity and seasonal workability must be addressed together.')
para('Immediate management decisions: confirm actual contract and governing revisions; freeze survey/design scope; resolve quantity and bearing/load queries; obtain evidenced supplier/yard/crew/vessel capacities; price and fund the full lifecycle; validate and approve a feasible completion/recovery strategy. No claim of outperforming Saipem/McDermott is supported. The quality standard here is traceable evidence, explicit gates, realistic dates and measurable delivery performance.')
heading('1. Source coverage and document precedence')
para('Latest batch:68uploads;67opened;52distinct contents;7distinct contents have no exact prior local hash match. New contents include chart.pdf, Stage27/30/31/32 workbooks and distinct Volume2/3 contents. The large preliminary PDF exceeded32MiB and was not reviewed. P13 previously opened76files with21distinct contents. A full file-by-file inventory is in the workbook; repeated bytes reuse earlier analysis and retain its limitations. This is not a claim that every table and historical attachment has received exhaustive numerical/contract review.')
para('chart.pdf is an image-only Gantt-like graphic at poor readable scale; it provides no extractable activity network. ticket.pdf from P13 is a travel booking; no project requirement or actual mobilisation/award was inferred, and personal booking details are excluded. The ZIP master-plan archive was opened/integrity-checked and member hashes indexed; archive contents do not establish engineering completion.')
para('BRRP-specific sources govern subject to the contract hierarchy and amendments. Sections1–3 titled Sump Caisson and SWLP Casing Replacement Project require explicit incorporation/applicability before adoption. The latest supplied extension notices end at23June2026submission/24June2026unpriced opening; later notices and actual opening remain unconfirmed. SCC copies and A3 are identical to earlier files; the announced revised versions are not positively identified. SVL12.3 was located in Combined3pp261–341 and replaces the earlier missing-list issue, subject to amendment and vendor-status checks.')
para('Source hierarchy is to be reconciled using B-4 and SCC1.2; SCC overrides GCC for their conflict. Do not adopt a bidder’s proposed hierarchy or concession from a query table when the company reply does not accept it. Preserve original source files and dated issued revisions; record deletions and amendment overlays rather than editing historical originals.')
heading('2. Bridge scope and quantity baseline')
tab(['Bridge','Type','ConstructionMT','DemolitionMT'],[[b[0],b[1],sum(b[2:6]),b[6]]for b in bridges])
para('Source-row construction totals1141MT versus printed1142MT, including landing-strengthening216versus217MT. Handrail1166versus1168m and grating718versus719m² also remain unresolved; demolition357MT and GI1274m² sum consistently. These are tender transcriptions, not released member/plate purchase quantities or verified module weights. MTO quantities must be rebuilt from accepted drawings and measured condition before procurement.')
para('Three replacement/new packages are ICW–ICG lower deck, ICP–ICG lower deck and BHS–SLQ. Seven strengthening packages retain their bridge-specific conditions and service interfaces. Upper/lower deck labels and NQO/NOQ nomenclature must be controlled. BHS demolition is a distinct engineered operation after the accepted service/support transition, not an assumed concurrent steel-removal allowance.')
heading('3. Engineering basis, deliverables and release')
for item,value,ref,act in basis:para(item+' — '+value+'. Source: '+ref+'. '+act+'.')
para('The Engineering DCI register contains170proposed bridge deliverables plus13platform assessment entries. IDs prefixedSHV are proposed management IDs, not issued source drawing numbers. Combined1Annexure1 calls for global deck assessmentsICP/ICG/ICW/BHS/SLQ and local checksWIS/NOQ/NQD/WIN/NC/SC1/SCA/SCF. Project applicability and naming need confirmation. Fifteen specific technical queries are recorded with source, owner and affected release in the Technical Queries sheet. The source new-bridge GAs are recorded separately; source indicative dimensions and source study utilisation ratios cannot substitute for checked project design.')
para('C8 document categoriesA/I/R differ from review dispositionsA/B/C. Mother-document submission/resubmission/approval statesS/R/A must be mapped per applicable row. General review is10working days, with longer listed first reviews for specified documents; subsequent reviews and MCI stages require their stated treatment. Stage-specific project DCI/MCI and submission staggering are essential. The P14 scenario uses10working-day allowances for selected bridge-review activities, without proving every comment/review iteration is included.')
para('Analysis must cover operating and temporary stages, load combinations, bridge/platform displacement, member/joint capacity, fatigue/VIV where applicable, bearing travel/thrust/temperature setting, landing/local deck adequacy and lift/transport/removal stages. Detail welds, bolts, tolerances, camber, corrosion protection and inspection access from accepted calculations. Independent checking, CRS closure, correct source revision and authorised release are mandatory gate evidence. No approved AFC drawing sheets are created by a register.')
heading('4. A–Z execution procedures')
for code,title,owner,inputs,method,evidence,kpi,source in streams:
 heading(code+' — '+title,2);para('Accountable role: '+owner+'. Inputs: '+inputs+'.');para('Procedure: '+method);para('Acceptance evidence: '+evidence+'.');para('Control: '+kpi+'. Source: '+source+'.')
heading('5. Workpack and daily production system')
para('The workbook defines120bridge/task workpacks across survey, engineering, material, fabrication, coating, loadout, supports, installation, service transfer, removal, punch and turnover. Each workpack requires verified quantities and a controlled evidence index. An applicability disposition is required when a generic task category does not apply. The screen returnsHOLD until all eight listed gates areYES; even then it returnsVERIFY EVIDENCE, not an authorised release. Only the designated authority can release accepted work.')
para('Six-week review removes constraints;14-day lookahead confirms material, access and capacity; daily meeting checks PTW, weather/SIMOPS and named workfront readiness. Log actual accepted quantities, crew-hours, nonproductive causes and rework against the IWP. Weekly forecast uses accepted output/productive crew-day only after sufficient comparable data exist. Separate productivity changes from changed scope and rework; do not divide aggregate steel tonnage by headcount and call it a verified installation duration.')
heading('6. Procurement, fabrication and marine execution')
para('Twenty-five proposed procurement packages consist of ten bridge-structural scopes and fifteen common materials/services. Each requires applicability, quantities/specification, PS/vendor approvals, price, dates, inspection and preservation. P14 does not issue any PO or book a vessel. Validate SVL12.3 product/location/status; reference-only list amendments do not erase bans or B3restrictions. Apply Corrigendum3 Melt&Pour/DVA and Form1 requirements by policy classification, not blanket assumptions about every item.')
para('Fabrication sequence: released shop pack and heat-traceable material → qualified personnel/process → cut/fit-up and temporary stability/distortion control → weld/NDT/repair closure → dimensional survey/trial fit → surface preparation/coating/curing → verified module weight/COG and preservation → independent release for loadout. A shared coating cell is explicit in the scenario; actual area, cure system and physical cell capacity must be verified. Yard bays are assumed available for new steel after the prior package’s welding phase; retained bay occupancy and NDT constraints require validation.')
para('Marine sequence: engineered module envelope → suitable vessel/actual-radius chart/deck/stability/positioning → cargo support and sea-fastening/voyage assurance → accepted loadout/certificates/audit → forecast/workfront go/no-go → transport and offshore receipt → pre-install support strengthening → lift and bearing landing/connection → accepted service transfer → engineered removal/backload → as-built survey and punch. PlanICG/ICP/BHSwrap strengthening before new placement as required. Transfer-crane minimum5tonnes is not proof of bridge-lift capacity; minimum60special-personnel accommodation is not total projectPOB validation.')
heading('7. Schedule method, results and recovery')
para('The schedule is a development-level integrated network, not a detailed constructability-validated L4baseline. All285activities have unique IDs and valid predecessors, the graph is acyclic and forward/backward passes obey FS0. Explicit resource queues cover two fabrication bays, one coating cell, three strengthening crews, one heavy-lift chain, one cargo chain, one service-transfer team and one removal team. Other capacities, shared platform access, POB and engineering/NDT labour are not fully modelled.')
para('Office work usesMonday–Friday without holidays; yard usesMonday–Saturday; offshore uses7days outside16May–15October and treats each offshore phase as indivisible within an open season. This is a planning exclusion, not an automatic contractual time extension. Vendor deliveries usecalendar days. Dates are half-open: finish is the next boundary after productive work; milestone dates lie on that boundary. Float is calendar-day latest-start slack to scenario completion, not approved contract float.')
tab(['Scenario','Inputs changed','Calculated completion'],[['BASE','2bays×4MT/day;45day steel supply',sched['finish']],['MORE_YARD','4bays×8MT/day;45day steel supply','2028-02-26'],['FAST_SUPPLY_MORE_YARD','4bays×8MT/day;15day steel supply','2028-02-26']])
para('All three scenarios preserve review allowances; none proves the12month target. The common sequence waits for campaign survey/basis then completes staged analysis/detail approvals before steelPO; this is deliberately conservative and must be tested against lawful independent packages and verified survey rolling releases. Ten design streams run in parallel without a verified staffing model, so the scenario is also optimistic about engineering capacity. It is neither a guaranteed upper bound nor lower bound.')
para('Recovery options to evaluate: independent early survey/design release boundaries; approved overlap in design preparation while respecting mother-document review states; compliant stock and supplier reservations with explicit commercial authority; validated higher bay/coating/NDT throughput; module/transport strategy and operations windows; separate service/strengthening crews where workfront/POB permits; alternate seasonal execution with contractual notice/relief. Price each option and rerun full dependencies. Do not compress mandatory inspections, cure times or review periods merely to achieve a date. No procurement or at-risk fabrication is authorised by this report.')
heading('8. Cost, cash and progress')
para('The control workbook records25cost accounts and156weekly cash periods, extendable to actual obligation expiry. Budgets, rates and cash inputs intentionally remain blank. These are operating templates, not a priced estimate or funded forecast. Cost EAC is actual paid plus all remaining expenditure, including accrued unpaid/commitments/uncommittedETC once, with no duplication. Cash separates receipts, retention/security releases, vendor/labour/marine/tax-finance and other flows. Weekly net cash is withheld until all eight input categories are numeric and the row is marked VERIFIED; enter explicit zero only for evidenced nil cash. Cumulative cash is withheld if any preceding week is incomplete. Opening cash must be funded and evidenced.')
para('Use amended A10milestones, not arbitrary revenue percentages. Earlier amendment deletes separateMob/Demobitems12/13 and revises repair-arrival20to25%; uploaded baseMPF still contains original lines. Reconcile the entire allocation before forecasting. Bid security extends45days beyond applicable bid validity; validity anchor and supporting-company guarantee dates follow corrigenda. Guarantee face value differs from margin cash and bank fees. Do not assume mobilisation advance, tax exemption, retention release or certificate/payment lags without terms.')
para('Engineering review dispositions and MCI stage weights apply only to their prescribed bases. Accepted physical work, certification, invoice, net collection and EV are separate measures. SPI/CPI require approvedPV/BAC/AC; no meaningful ratio is available from zero/missing inputs. Daily e-MBmeasurements and approvedSESlinks are billing prerequisites underSCC12. Monthly critical-event logs and quarterly joint delay analysis are deliverables; the workbooks do not upload them automatically.')
heading('9. Risk, assurance and completion')
for r in risks:para(r[0]+' — '+r[1]+'. Warning: '+r[2]+'. Owner: '+r[3]+'. Response: '+r[4]+'. Gate: '+r[5]+'.')
para('Risk likelihood/cost/schedule impacts remain unquantified; no probability orP80claim is made. Use project-specific operating/abort limits and maintain actual weather, vessel/master decisions, standby causes and personnel accountability. Evaluate DGS/company audit provisions at mobilisation date. HSEandQAauthorities retain stop-work authority; management acceleration does not override the release gates.')
para('Turnover is bridge/system based: structural/bearing inspection and accepted dimensions, weld/NDT/coating/material records, service reinstatement/tests and operations acceptance, scrap transport/yard receipt, native/as-built/vendor dossiers and punch closure. Commissioning is scoped to affected bridge services and interfaces; generic platform specifications do not automatically add full new process systems. Separate structural/mechanical completion, ready-for-service, company handover, final account and continuing warranty/security/integrity-pact obligations.')
heading('10. First90days and issue acceptance')
para('Relative management targets areD1contract/spending basis,D7named organisation,D15capacity/supplier offers,D30survey/basis and validated scheduling plan,D45first independently acceptable release where achievable,D60funded procurement/released production,D75measured productivity/marine assurance andD90integrated feasibility decision. These targets are not represented as achieved. P14base engineering release is later thanD45; therefore early-release objectives need a justified alternative sequence and capacity decision.')
para('Accept the management baseline only after the actual start and controlling contract revisions are known, scope/MTO discrepancies resolved or explicitly dispositioned, design release logic accepted, supplier dates and resources evidenced, seasonal feasibility evaluated, control budget/cash funded and approvals signed. Until then useP14as the single development-control index with versioned updates. Keep source issuesP8–P13for audit references; retire conflicting working schedules only after an authorised baseline decision.')
heading('11. Deliverables and limits of completion')
para('Delivered: this execution manual inWord/PDF; integratedExcelcontrol workbook;285activityCSV; readable bridge/phase schedulePDF; deterministic scenario data/scripts and source coverage inventories. Registers provide structured execution requirements, evidence and actions. The requested project-management development work is carried forward comprehensively; actual engineering certification, approvedAFCs, orders/charters, fabrication, installation, testing, commissioning and accepted project completion are not performed by preparing this package.')
para('No more missing-data approval question is needed to issue these reviewable documents. Subsequent commitments and construction releases must use the authorised contractual/technical decision process and real evidence. User-supplied files are treated as references; no external emails, portal submissions, declarations or orders were executed.')
